  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far is config_005 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) at 0.650 accuracy. We know avgpool outperformed transformer for pca_n2000 (0.591 vs 0.519), and scvi_n200 outperformed both pca_n2000 and scgpt under avgpool. However, we have not tested whether the aggregation preference (avgpool > transformer) is encoder-dependent—scvi_n200 produces a learned latent representation that may interact differently with transformer attention than with simple averaging. This experiment (config_006) is a single-variable change from config_005 (avgpool → transformer), cleanly isolating the aggregation effect under the best encoder. If it beats 0.650, we find a new best; if not, we confirm avgpool is optimal for scvi_n200 and can confidently direct the remaining 3 experiments toward testing whether multimodal fusion (with a stronger ViT-L image encoder) can add value on top of the best RNA-only setup, rather than wasting budget on suboptimal aggregation choices."
}

